Use this decision tree:

Workload Failed
     |
     +-- Pod issue?
     |
     +-- Scheduler issue?
     |
     +-- Node Ready?
     |
     +-- OS healthy?
     |
     +-- GPU healthy?
     |
     +-- Fabric healthy?
     |
     +-- Storage reachable?
     |
     +-- Network healthy?
     |
     +-- Monitoring showing hardware alarm?

Useful Kubernetes commands:

kubectl get pods -A
kubectl describe pod POD
kubectl logs POD
kubectl get nodes
kubectl describe node NODE
kubectl get events -A
